  "body": "As of today, it fails with a\n\n> ART/rtengine/dcraw.cc:26:16: fatal error: 'omp.h' file not found\n>    26 | /*RT*/#include <omp.h>\n>       |                ^~~~~~~\n> \n\nHowever OpenMP is correctly installed and found by CMake:\n\n> -- Found OpenMP_C: -Xclang -fopenmp (found version \"5.1\")\n> -- Found OpenMP_CXX: -Xclang -fopenmp (found version \"5.1\")\n> -- Found OpenMP: TRUE (found version \"5.1\")\n\nHowever I have noticed that when the error is issued, the very long command line /usr/bin/c++ doesn't include the location of the OpenMP header files. Even though CMakeCache.txt contains:\n\n> OpenMP_CXX_INCLUDE_DIR:PATH=/opt/homebrew/include\n\nwhich is the right path of omp.h \n\n\nThere's also another error right at the start of the compilation:\n\n> [1/298] Creating AboutThisBuild.txt and other version-dependent files\n> -- git command found: /opt/homebrew/bin/git\n> fatal: no tag exactly matches '091d8b74ecc2e1cfe82b36db1ca2c856aac39f9b'\n> -- Git checkout information:\n> --     Commit description: 091d8b74e\n> --     Branch: master\n> --     Commit: 091d8b74e\n> --     Commit date: 2026-04-08\n\nOf course /opt/homebrew/bin/git exists and it's a symlink to the real git (otherwise how could I pull the sources...)\n\nAnd there's also another git which ships with Mac OS in /usr/bin/git ",
